    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "To the hundreds of millions of “Swifties” around the world, Taylor Swift means much more than just great music. She’s also a source of strength. Two Chinese “Swifties” share their stories here."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "h1",
        "type": "heading",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Huang Shiyao, 25"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "My love for Taylor Swift began when I was 14. Her songs lit a fire in me, "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "fuelling",
            "ref": "v-fuel"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " my dream of one day living in a big city. Taylor grew up in a small town in Pennsylvania. At the age of 14, she moved to a larger city to chase her dream of becoming a musician. If she could spread her wings, why couldn’t I?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "My family didn’t expect much of me because I was a girl. They only hoped I would get married and have children, not chase my own ambitions. Taylor’s songs encouraged me to work hard and create more opportunities for myself."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Many of Taylor’s songs speak out against "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "gender bias",
            "zh": "性别偏见"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Take "
          },
          {
            "t": "em",
            "v": "The Man"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", for example. It points out how women are often judged "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "unfairly",
            "ref": "v-unfairly"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". It reminds me of a female teacher at my university who is good at programming. Who says only men can shine in STEM subjects?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "h2",
        "type": "heading",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Huang Weijie, 20"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "It has been seven years since I first watched Taylor Swift’s music videos. Back then, I was simply drawn in by her voice and beauty. But over time, I discovered something deeper."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "I appreciate how Taylor pours her emotions and real-life experiences into her "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "lyrics",
            "ref": "v-lyric"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Thanks to her, I started writing down my own feelings and, along the way, I learnt to love myself more."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p7",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Taylor also gave me confidence. In middle school, I was overweight. My classmates teased me, calling me fat. To lose weight, I ate very little. That left me sleepy all day and unable to focus on my studies."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p8",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "In her 2020 "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "documentary",
            "ref": "v-documentary"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " "
          },
          {
            "t": "em",
            "v": "Miss Americana"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", Taylor spoke openly about body image. She said that she once stopped eating to improve her looks, but later found that it was damaging to her health. Her words taught me that there isn’t just one way to be beautiful. Health is worth more than a “perfect” body."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
